.TH "Tubeup" "1" "June 2026" "Multi\-VOD uploader to Archive.org" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\f[B]tubeup\f[R] \(em A multi\-VOD service to Archive.org uploader
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tubeup\f[R] [[URL]]\f[B]|\f[R][USERNAME]\f[B]|\f[R][[PASSWORD]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Use yt\-dlp to download video/metadata and upload to the Internet
Archive.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
<url>
yt\-dlp compatible URL to download.
Check yt\-dlp documentation for a list of compatible websites.
.TP
\-\-metadata=<key:value>
Custom metadata to add to the archive.org item.
.TP
\-\-dir <dir>
Provide a directory for downloads and metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\-h, \(enhelp
Show this screen
.TP
\-x, \-\-proxy <prox>
Use a proxy while uploading
.TP
\-u, \-\-username <user>
Provide a username, for sites like Nico Nico Douga
.TP
\-p, \-\-password <pass>
Provide a password, for sites like Nico Nico Douga
.TP
\-a, \-\-use\-download\-archive
Record the video url to the download archive.
This will download only videos not listed in the archive file.
Also records the ID\(cqs of all downloaded videos
.TP
\-q, \-\-quiet
Just print errors
.TP
\-d, \-\-debug
Print all logs to stdout
.TP
\-o, \-\-output <output>
yt\-dlp output template
.TP
\-i, \-\-ignore\-existing\-item
Don\(cqt check if an item already exists on archive.org
